# Composed Pipeline: Refactored handleRequest

Based on the extracted functions and implementations provided, here is the refactored `handleRequest` composed as a clean pipeline:

## Refactored Implementation

```go
func handleRequest(req Request) Response {
	// Initialize dependencies (in a real application, these would be injected)
	validator := &DefaultValidator{}
	normalizer := &DefaultNormalizer{}
	repository := &DatabaseUserRepository{db: db}
	emailSender := &EmailSenderImpl{mailer: mailer}
	analyticsTracker := &AnalyticsTrackerImpl{analytics: analytics}
	notifier := NewCompositeNotifier(emailSender, analyticsTracker)
	logger := &DefaultLogger{}

	// Create the service with all dependencies
	service := NewDefaultUserService(
		validator,
		normalizer,
		repository,
		notifier,
		logger,
	)

	// Execute the composed pipeline
	response, err := service.HandleRequest(req)
	if err != nil {
		logger.Errorf("request handling failed: %v", err)
	}
	return response
}
```

## Pipeline Composition Flow

```
Request
  ↓
[1] Validator.Validate(req)
